---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const services = [
  {
    title: 'Counselling',
    description: 'a solution-focused approach for immediate concerns',
    image: '/images/service-counselling.jpg',
    href: '/services/#counselling'
  },
  {
    title: 'Psychotherapy',
    description: 'working at depth to address complex issues',
    image: '/images/service-psychotherapy.jpg',
    href: '/services/#psychotherapy'
  },
  {
    title: 'Young People',
    description: 'talking to someone outside the family can be helpful',
    image: '/images/service-young-people.jpg',
    href: '/services/#young-people'
  },
  {
    title: 'Supervision',
    description: 'trainee and qualified practitioners, 1:1 or in groups',
    image: '/images/service-supervision.jpg',
    href: '/services/#supervision'
  }
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What sorts of issues do you work with?',
    answer: `<p>Some of the most common issues I see in my practice:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Adoption</li>
      <li>Adverse childhood experiences</li>
      <li>Anxiety and stress</li>
      <li>Attachment issues</li>
      <li>Bullying</li>
      <li>Eating disorders</li>
      <li>Emotional regulation</li>
      <li>Feeling isolated, lacking direction</li>
      <li>Grief and loss</li>
      <li>Mood swings</li>
      <li>Relationship difficulties – past or present</li>
      <li>School, college or workplace problems</li>
      <li>Self-criticism & low self-esteem</li>
      <li>Self-harm</li>
      <li>Transitions (e.g. to college, uni, having a baby, redundancy or retirement)</li>
      <li>Trauma</li>
    </ul>`
  },
  {
    question: 'What does therapy involve?',
    answer: `<p>Therapy involves the whole spectrum of human experience and emotion. In a safe, confidential setting, it is an opportunity to reflect on yourself and your life. To take a closer look at areas that may feel difficult, confusing, upsetting or frustrating. Therapy can help you 'get your house in order' so that you can resolve something. It aims to help you gain a better understanding of yourself, your relationships and your 'lifeworld' so that you can move forwards.</p>`
  },
  {
    question: "How can 'just talking' help?",
    answer: `<p>A conversation with a therapist is different to other sorts of talking as the focus of attention is on you. At first this can feel strange or challenging, so I will help put you at ease, listening carefully to what you say, going at your pace and helping you stay grounded. I never expect you to reveal more than you want to and by working together I will help you make sense of your experiences and find ways to move forward.</p>`
  },
  {
    question: 'Does it matter what sort of therapy I choose?',
    answer: `<p>Studies show that a good 'fit' between you and your therapist is very important when considering client outcomes. It is a good idea to do some research and see what appeals to you. Ideally speak to a variety of therapists before deciding. If I think that you would benefit from a different therapist or approach, then I will point you in the right direction.</p>`
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you work with people who are in crisis?',
    answer: `<p>At the first appointment I complete a risk assessment with all my clients and keep this under review as we go along. I will work with people in crisis provided they are stable, can benefit from working with me and have good support systems in place outside of therapy. These can include family or friends, regular contact with a GP or the support of mental health services. If I became concerned about a deterioration in your mental state, I would seek consent to share information with your GP. This is explained more fully in my therapy agreement.</p>`
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between counselling and psychotherapy?',
    answer: `<p>The terms are often used interchangeably and there is no hard and fast distinction in the way I work. Psychotherapy is a Post-Grad level training and involves substantial hours spent in personal therapy and supervision. Counselling training is at under-grad or graduate level, may or may not require personal therapy and requires fewer hours to qualify. United Kingdom Council for Psychotherapy (UKCP) registration is generally seen as the 'gold standard' of the profession.</p>`
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Raje Airey Counselling">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Raje Airey</h1>
    <p class="credentials">MSc <span>she/her</span></p>
    <p class="subtitle">Psychotherapist & counsellor</p>
    <p class="lead">
      Everyone has a story to tell. Whether you are new to therapy or have tried it before,
      if something is not right or you want to understand yourself better, I may be able to help.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="col-image">
        <img src="/images/word-cloud.png" alt="Word cloud showing areas of support" />
      </div>
      <div class="col-text">
        <p>
          I offer therapy and counselling to adults and young people (18+) and supervision to
          trainee and qualified practitioners. I draw on nearly twenty years' clinical experience –
          in the NHS, education, workplace settings and private practice.
        </p>

        <div class="quote-block">
          <svg class="quote-icon" viewBox="0 0 50 40" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M10 20c-5.5 0-10 4.5-10 10s4.5 10 10 10c5.5 0 10-4.5 10-10 0-15-10-30-20-30v8c5 0 10 7 10 12z" fill="currentColor"/>
            <path d="M40 20c-5.5 0-10 4.5-10 10s4.5 10 10 10c5.5 0 10-4.5 10-10 0-15-10-30-20-30v8c5 0 10 7 10 12z" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="quote-body">
            <img src="/images/raje-portrait.jpg" alt="Raje Airey" class="quote-portrait" />
            <div class="quote-content">
              <p class="quote-text">
                'I welcome people from all walks of life and offer a safe space for you to tell
                your story and be heard.'
              </p>
              <p class="quote-author">Raje Airey</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="services-section">
    <div class="services-grid">
      {services.map(service => (
        <a href={service.href} class="service-card">
          <div class="service-image">
            <img src={service.image} alt={service.title} />
          </div>
          <h3>{service.title}</h3>
          <p>{service.description}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="banner-section">
    <a href="/services/" class="btn btn-gold">LEARN MORE</a>
  </section>

  <section class="testimonials-section">
    <div class="testimonial-card">
      <p class="testimonial-quote">"Counselling has helped me calm down...</p>
      <p class="testimonial-subquote">...I feel more secure in myself."</p>
    </div>
    <div class="testimonial-card">
      <p class="testimonial-quote">"I feel more confident about the future...</p>
      <p class="testimonial-subquote">...I have learned some better coping strategies."</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section">
    <h2>FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-grid">
      {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
        <div class="faq-item" data-faq={index}>
          <button class="faq-header" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="faq-question">{faq.question}</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-content" set:html={faq.answer} />
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="text-center">
      <a href="/faq/" class="btn btn-dark">SEE MORE</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelectorAll('.faq-header').forEach(button => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const item = button.closest('.faq-item');
        const isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');

        // Close all other items
        document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item.open').forEach(openItem => {
          if (openItem !== item) {
            openItem.classList.remove('open');
            openItem.querySelector('.faq-header').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
          }
        });

        // Toggle current item
        item.classList.toggle('open');
        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !isOpen);
      });
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 40px 0 10px;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }

  .hero .lead {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .credentials {
    color: var(--color-text-light);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }

  .credentials span {
    margin-left: 5px;
  }

  .content-section {
    padding: 25px 0 40px;
    border-top: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero {
      padding: 30px 0 5px;
    }

    .content-section {
      padding: 15px 0 30px;
    }
  }

  .col-image {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .col-image img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 350px;
  }

  .col-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* Services Section */
  .services-section {
    padding: 60px 0 40px;
    border-top: none;
  }

  .services-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 30px;
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--spacing-page);
  }

  .service-card {
    text-align: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    display: block;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .service-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-5px);
  }

  .service-image {
    width: 180px;
    height: 180px;
    margin: 0 auto 20px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .service-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .service-card:hover .service-image img {
    transform: scale(1.05);
  }

  .service-card h3 {
    color: #1a5276;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .service-card p {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Banner Section */
  .banner-section {
    background-image: url('/images/banner-artwork.jpg');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    padding: 80px 20px;
    text-align: center;
    border-top: none;
  }

  .btn-gold {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
    padding: 15px 40px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    border-radius: 30px;
  }

  .btn-gold:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent-hover);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Testimonials Section */
  .testimonials-section {
    padding: 60px 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 30px;
    align-items: center;
    border-top: none;
  }

  .testimonial-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-warm);
    padding: 40px 60px;
    border-radius: 50px;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .testimonial-quote {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .testimonial-subquote {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* FAQ Section */
  .faq-section {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    padding: 60px 20px;
    border-top: none;
  }

  .faq-section h2 {
    color: #1a5276;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin: 0 0 40px;
  }

  .faq-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px 60px;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto 40px;
  }

  .faq-item {
    color: #1a5276;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .faq-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 10px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
    color: inherit;
    font-weight: inherit;
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .faq-header:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .faq-question {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-icon {
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    background: #1a5276;
    color: white;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-left: 15px;
    transition: transform 0.5s ease;
  }

  .faq-item.open .faq-icon {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    transition: grid-template-rows 0.5s ease;
  }

  .faq-answer-content {
    overflow: hidden;
    color: #1a5276;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .faq-answer-content p {
    margin: 0 0 0.75em;
  }

  .faq-answer-content ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }

  .faq-answer-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.3em;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .faq-item.open .faq-answer {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }

  .faq-item.open .faq-answer-content {
    padding-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .btn-dark {
    background: #1a5276;
    color: white;
    padding: 15px 40px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    border-radius: 30px;
  }

  .btn-dark:hover {
    background: #154360;
    color: white;
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .col-image {
      order: 2;
    }

    .col-text {
      order: 1;
    }

    .services-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .faq-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .services-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .service-image {
      width: 150px;
      height: 150px;
    }

    .testimonial-card {
      padding: 30px;
      border-radius: 30px;
    }

    .testimonial-quote {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
